link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/us-rejects-irans-claim-of-capturing-underwater-drone-calls-move-clearly-desperate/articleshow/134523402.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T22:07:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134523514,imgsize-496310.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Yellowstone rangers remove 20,100 pieces of trash from geothermal areas in 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134523257.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Yellowstone rangers removed more than 20,100 pieces of trash from geothermal areas in 2026, along with over 5,000 rocks and sticks and 280 visitor hats. Staff also collected coins worth more than $18. Among the unusual finds were AirPods, golf tees, an inhaler, Invisalign retainers, fake nails and children’s toys.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/yellowstone-rangers-remove-20100-pieces-of-trash-from-geothermal-areas-in-2026-including-more-than-5000-rocks-and-sticks-280-visitor-hats-and-over-18-in-coins/articleshow/134523257.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/yellowstone-rangers-remove-20100-pieces-of-trash-from-geothermal-areas-in-2026-including-more-than-5000-rocks-and-sticks-280-visitor-hats-and-over-18-in-coins/articleshow/134523257.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T21:54:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134523309,imgsize-102643.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pennsylvania teacher’s $5,000 donation helps turn China’s Maowusu desert into a forest of 50,000 trees]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134522082.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pennsylvania teacher Ronald Sakolsky reunited with Chinese farmer Yin Yuzhen 26 years after donating $5,000 to support her tree-planting efforts in Inner Mongolia. His contribution helped Yin expand her work in the Maowusu Desert, which has since become a forest of around 50,000 trees, turning their friendship into an enduring environmental story.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/in-1999-pennsylvania-teacher-ronald-sakolsky-donated-5000-to-farmer-yin-yuzhen-to-fund-her-tree-planting-efforts-in-inner-mongolia-27-years-later-his-contribution-helped-transform-chinas-maowusu-desert-into-a-forest-of-50000-trees/articleshow/134522082.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/in-1999-pennsylvania-teacher-ronald-sakolsky-donated-5000-to-farmer-yin-yuzhen-to-fund-her-tree-planting-efforts-in-inner-mongolia-27-years-later-his-contribution-helped-transform-chinas-maowusu-desert-into-a-forest-of-50000-trees/articleshow/134522082.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T20:25:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134522102,imgsize-173066.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2020, a New Jersey man lost his job and began mowing lawns for free; six years later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134521228.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After losing his job, Brian Schwartz founded a remarkable volunteer initiative named I Want To Mow Your Lawn. This program offers complimentary lawn care services to seniors, veterans, and others in need. Through a digital platform, volunteers across all 50 states now connect with those requiring assistance, resulting in a thriving community of over 2,000 compassionate participants who collectively enhance the spirit of service and support nationwide.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-new-jersey-man-lost-his-job-and-began-mowing-lawns-for-free-six-years-later-his-volunteer-network-has-grown-to-more-than-2000-people-across-all-50-us-states/articleshow/134521228.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-new-jersey-man-lost-his-job-and-began-mowing-lawns-for-free-six-years-later-his-volunteer-network-has-grown-to-more-than-2000-people-across-all-50-us-states/articleshow/134521228.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T20:22:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134522163,imgsize-1072669.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[$888 million for ads: US Republicans ramp up sends to defend 39 House seats once deemed 'safe']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134521408.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Republicans are investing significantly in House races previously deemed secure as they confront emerging electoral challenges. Spending has surged to $888 million in advertising compared to $666 million by Democrats. Economic pressures are impacting traditionally Republican districts and may influence voter sentiments. Republican strategists are concerned about potential losses and are campaigning vigorously. Maintaining their House majority is now a priority for GOP leaders ahead of the elections.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/888-million-for-ads-us-republicans-ramp-up-sends-to-defend-39-house-seats-once-deemed-safe/articleshow/134521408.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/888-million-for-ads-us-republicans-ramp-up-sends-to-defend-39-house-seats-once-deemed-safe/articleshow/134521408.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T19:30:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134521512,imgsize-228834.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['American terrorist army': Iran claims second US submarine seized in Hormuz]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134521244.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/american-terrorist-army-iran-claims-second-us-submarine-seized-in-hormuz/articleshow/134521244.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/american-terrorist-army-iran-claims-second-us-submarine-seized-in-hormuz/articleshow/134521244.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-27T19:08:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134521295,imgsize-518452.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2018, Jon Bon Jovi paid $10 million for a Palm Beach home, demolished it and rebuilt; 2 years later]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134520276.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jon Bon Jovi recently sold his exquisite Palm Beach residence for nearly $20 million, a significant increase from the $10 million he initially invested in the land. On the same day, he invested $43 million in a lavish oceanfront property extending over 10,000 square feet, featuring high-end amenities such as a swimming pool and private courtyard. This move underlines the increasing demand for luxury real estate in Palm Beach.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.i